NNAAMMEE
       error - Postfix error/retry mail delivery agent

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       eerrrroorr [generic Postfix daemon options]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  Postfix  eerrrroorr(8)  delivery agent processes delivery requests from
       the queue manager. Each request specifies a queue file,  a  sender  ad‐
       dress,  the reason for non-delivery (specified as the next-hop destina‐
       tion), and recipient information.  The reason may be prefixed  with  an
       RFC  3463-compatible  detail code; if none is specified a default 4.0.0
       or 5.0.0 code is used instead.  This program expects to be run from the
       mmaasstteerr(8) process manager.

       Depending on the service name in master.cf, eerrrroorr or rreettrryy, the  server
       bounces  or  defers  all  recipients  in the delivery request using the
       "next-hop" information as the reason for non-delivery. The  rreettrryy  ser‐
       vice name is supported as of Postfix 2.4.

       Delivery status reports are sent to the bboouunnccee(8), ddeeffeerr(8) or ttrraaccee(8)
       daemon as appropriate.

SSEECCUURRIITTYY
       The  eerrrroorr(8) mailer is not security-sensitive. It does not talk to the
       network, and can be run chrooted at fixed low privilege.

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
       RFC 3463 (Enhanced Status Codes)

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
       Problems and transactions are logged to ssyyssllooggdd(8) or ppoossttllooggdd(8).

       Depending on the setting of the nnoottiiffyy__ccllaasssseess parameter, the  postmas‐
       ter is notified of bounces and of other trouble.

